    "sine_linearization_bias_remains": "For constant m=1 and R=128, the ideal R/(2*pi)*sin(2*pi*m/R) bias is about 4.02e-4; recovering odd terms does not remove it.",
    "h32_limitation": "Four independent-key N=8192 probes, including pilot: three candidates passed 1e-3, one failed catastrophically (max error 88.9760141301). Not a failure-rate estimate. Failure ciphertext was not saved, so root cause is not established.",
    "ratio_limitation": "N=65536 R=1024 misses 2e-5 on constant; R=2048 misses 2e-5 for all six distributions. N=8192 successes do not validate these ratios at N=65536.",
